            <ArticleTitle>Myriads: p-value-based multiple testing correction.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/bioinformatics/btx746</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="Motivation" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">There are many multiple testing correction methods. Some of them are robust to various dependencies in the data while others are not. Some of the implementations have problems for managing high dimensional list of p-values as currently demanded by microarray and other omic technologies.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="Results" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">The program Myriads, formerly SGoF+, provides some of the most important p-value-based correction methods jointly with a test of dependency and a p-value simulator. Myriads easily manages hundreds of thousands of p-values.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="Availability" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">http://myriads.webs.uvigo.es.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="Contact" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">myriads@uvigo.es.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="Supplementary information" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">Supplementary data are available at Bioinformatics online.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
